-- legal_search_mock food_safety_2026 — init.sql
-- A synthesized food-safety/online-shopping consumer punitive-damages dispute research corpus for a litigation benchmark:
-- • 6 courts across Shanghai/Zhejiang (including Shanghai Pudong Court, the court at the online-shopping place of receipt + Hangzhou Court, the court where the seller is located + the court where the e-commerce platform is located)
-- • 4 statutes: Food Safety Law + Law on the Protection of Consumer Rights and Interests + Civil Code + Supreme People's Court Judicial Interpretation on Food and Drug Disputes
-- • 18 anonymized food-safety/online-shopping contract judgments (refund plus tenfold compensation / ten times the purchase price or three times the loss / 1000 yuan minimum guarantee /
-- Knowingly buying counterfeit food is still compensable in the food sector / imported food without a Chinese-language label / past its shelf life / illegal additives / label defects are not compensable / choose either the producer or the seller /
-- Platform joint liability or advance compensation / online-shopping jurisdiction at the place of receipt ...)
--   • citation links from cases → statute articles (and a few case→case references)
-- • Seeded user usr_zhao_meng with 2 saved cases + notes (preparing a food-safety punitive-damages lawsuit)
-- All party names anonymized (Zhang [surname]/a certain company). All text original/synthesized; statute text
-- simplified public-domain-style. Reference date: 2026-05-20 (scenario reference; server has no clock).

BEGIN;

-- ── Courts / Courts ───────────────────────────────────────────────────

-- ── Statutes ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    'Regulates food production and operations, labeling, requirements for imported food, and legal liability. Article 148 provides that where food that does not meet food safety standards is produced, or food known not to meet food safety standards is sold, consumers may, in addition to seeking compensation for losses, demand punitive compensation from the producer or seller in the amount of ten times the purchase price or three times the loss; if the increased compensation is less than 1,000 yuan, it shall be calculated as 1,000 yuan. This does not apply where defects in food labels or instructions do not affect food safety and will not mislead consumers.'),
  ('stat_cpl_consumer', 'Law of the People''s Republic of China on the Protection of Consumer Rights and Interests', 'Consumer Rights and Interests Protection Law', 'Standing Committee of the National People''s Congress', '2014-03-15', 'Currently in force',
    'Protect consumers’ lawful rights and interests. Article 55 stipulates that where a business operator commits fraud in providing goods or services, it shall provide additional compensation equal to three times the price paid by the consumer; if the additional compensation is less than 500 yuan, it shall be 500 yuan (triple compensation for ordinary consumer goods). The relevant liabilities of e-commerce platform operators are also stipulated.'),
  ('stat_ccl',  'Civil Code of the People''s Republic of China', 'Civil Code', 'National People''s Congress', '2021-01-01', 'Currently in force',
    'Regulates the personal and property relations of civil subjects, including core provisions in the Contracts Book (sales contracts and liability for breach of contract), the Tort Liability Book (product liability, producer and seller liability, and punitive damages), and the General Provisions Book (a three-year statute of limitations).'),
  ('stat_interp','Provisions of the Supreme People''s Court on Several Issues Concerning the Application of Law in the Trial of Food and Drug Dispute Cases', 'Provisions on Food and Drug Disputes', 'The Supreme People''s Court', '2021-01-01', 'Currently in force',
    'Clarifying the rules for adjudicating food and drug disputes: When a purchaser knowingly buys food that does not meet safety standards and seeks punitive damages, the defense that the purchaser knew about the issue is not valid in the food and drug sectors, and the people''s court will not support that defense (i.e., “knowingly buying counterfeit goods” does not affect the right to claim compensation); this also covers the liability of online trading platforms and the concurrence of the compensation liabilities of producers and sellers, among other matters.');

-- ── Statute articles ─────────────────────────────────────────
-- Key articles of the Food Safety Law
    'A consumer who suffers harm from food that does not meet food safety standards may demand compensation for the loss from the seller or producer. Where a producer manufactures food that does not meet food safety standards, or a seller knowingly sells food that does not meet food safety standards, the consumer may, in addition to demanding compensation for the loss, also demand from the producer or seller punitive compensation equal to ten times the price paid or three times the loss; if the increased compensation is less than 1,000 yuan, it shall be 1,000 yuan. However, this does not apply where the food’s labels or instructions contain defects that do not affect food safety and do not mislead consumers.'),
  ('art_fsl_097', 'stat_fsl', 'Article 97', 97, 'Chinese labels for imported prepackaged food',
    'Imported prepackaged foods and food additives shall bear labels in Chinese; where instructions are required by law, they shall also include instructions in Chinese. The labels and instructions shall comply with this Law, other relevant Chinese laws and administrative regulations, and the requirements of national food safety standards, and shall state the food’s country of origin and the name, address, and contact information of the domestic agent. Prepackaged foods without labels or instructions in Chinese, or whose labels or instructions do not comply with this Article, shall not be imported.'),
  ('art_fsl_034', 'stat_fsl', 'Article 34', 34, 'Foods prohibited from being produced or sold (expired/illegal additives, etc.)',
    'The production and sale of the following foods are prohibited: foods produced using non-food raw materials, or foods to which chemical substances other than food additives or other substances that may endanger human health have been added; foods past their expiration date; foods bearing false production dates or shelf lives, or foods past their expiration date; unlabeled prepackaged foods; and other foods that do not comply with food safety standards or requirements.'),
  ('art_fsl_150', 'stat_fsl', 'Article 150', 150, 'The meaning of food safety and food safety standards',
    'Food safety means that food is nontoxic and harmless, meets the nutritional requirements it should have, and causes no acute, subacute, or chronic harm to human health. Food-safety standards are mandatory standards.');

-- Key articles of the Consumer Rights Protection Law
    'Where a business operator engages in fraudulent conduct in providing goods or services, it shall, at the consumer’s request, increase the compensation for the consumer’s losses; the increased compensation shall be three times the price paid for the goods purchased or the fees paid for the services received. If the increased compensation is less than 500 yuan, it shall be 500 yuan. Note: In the field of food safety, the punitive compensation under Article 148 of the Food Safety Law (ten times/ minimum of 1,000 yuan) takes precedence and differs from the three-times/500-yuan rule under this Article.'),
  ('art_cpl_c_44', 'stat_cpl_consumer', 'Article 44', 44, 'Online trading platform liability',
    'Where a consumer purchases goods or accepts services through an online trading platform and their lawful rights and interests are harmed, the consumer may demand compensation from the seller or service provider. If the online trading platform provider cannot provide the seller’s or service provider’s real name, address, and effective contact information, the consumer may also demand compensation from the online trading platform provider. If the online trading platform provider makes a commitment more favorable to consumers, it must fulfill that commitment. If the platform knows or should know that a seller has infringed consumers’ lawful rights and interests but fails to take necessary measures, it shall bear joint and several liability with the seller in accordance with the law.');

-- Key articles of the Civil Code
    'The limitation period for bringing a lawsuit to request that a people''s court protect civil rights is three years. Where the law provides otherwise, those provisions shall apply. The limitation period begins to run from the date when the right holder knew or should have known both that the right had been infringed and who the obligor was.'),
  ('art_ccl_1203', 'stat_ccl', 'Article 1203', 1203, 'Product liability (concurrent compensation claims against producers and sellers)',
    'If a defective product causes harm to another person, the infringed party may seek compensation from either the product''s producer or its seller. If the defect was caused by the producer, the seller, after paying compensation, has the right to seek recourse from the producer; if the defect was caused by the seller''s fault, the producer, after paying compensation, has the right to seek recourse from the seller.'),
  ('art_ccl_509', 'stat_ccl', 'Article 509', 509, 'Principle of contract performance',
    'The parties shall fully perform their respective obligations as agreed. The parties shall follow the principle of good faith and, in accordance with the nature and purpose of the contract and trade practices, perform obligations such as notification, assistance, and confidentiality.');

-- Key articles of the Supreme People’s Court Provisions on Food and Drug Disputes
    'When a dispute arises due to the quality of food or drugs, and the purchaser asserts rights against the producer or seller, the people''s court shall not support a defense by the producer or seller that the purchaser knowingly bought the food or drugs despite being aware of the quality problem. That is, in the food and drug sectors, whether the purchaser "knowingly bought counterfeit or substandard goods" does not affect their right to claim punitive damages in accordance with the law.'),
  ('art_interp_06', 'stat_interp', 'Article 6', 6, 'Advance compensation by online trading platforms and joint and several liability',
    'Where a consumer purchases food or medicine through an online trading platform and their lawful rights and interests are harmed, if the online trading platform provider cannot provide the producer’s or seller’s real name, address, and effective contact information, a consumer’s request for the online trading platform provider to bear liability for compensation shall be supported by the people’s court. After bearing liability for compensation, the online trading platform provider has the right to seek recourse from the producer or seller. If the platform knows or should know that a seller is using the platform to infringe consumers’ rights and interests but fails to take necessary measures, it shall bear joint and several liability with the seller.'),
  ('art_interp_15', 'stat_interp', 'Article 15', 15, 'Minor labeling defects that do not affect safety and are not misleading are excluded.',
    'Where the food produced and sold complies with food safety standards, but its label or instructions contain defects that do not affect food safety and will not mislead consumers, a consumer’s request for punitive damages equal to ten times the purchase price shall not be supported by the people’s court. In other words, tenfold punitive damages do not apply where the only issue is a labeling defect that neither affects food safety nor misleads consumers.');

-- ── Cases (anonymized judgments) ────────────────────────────────────
    'Plaintiff: Zhang Mou (consumer); Defendant: a certain food company (seller)',
    'When food purchased online by a consumer had passed its shelf life upon delivery, the court ordered a refund of the purchase price and punitive compensation equal to ten times the purchase price.',
    'Zhang Mou purchased a batch of imported biscuits from the defendant on an e-commerce platform for 800 yuan. Upon delivery, Zhang Mou discovered that the shelf life indicated based on the production date had expired one month earlier. Zhang Mou is claiming a refund plus ten times the purchase price. The defendant knowingly sold food that was past its shelf life.',
    'Under Article 34 of the Food Safety Law, food past its shelf life is food that does not meet food safety standards and is prohibited from sale. Under Article 148, where a business knowingly sells food that does not meet food safety standards, consumers may claim compensation equal to ten times the purchase price. The purchase price was 800 yuan, and ten times that amount is 8,000 yuan. As this exceeds the 1,000-yuan minimum, 8,000 yuan should be awarded, and the 800-yuan purchase price should also be refunded.',
    'Where a business operator sells food that is past its shelf life or otherwise does not comply with food safety standards, the consumer may claim a refund of the purchase price and compensation equal to ten times the purchase price.',
    '1. The defendant shall refund the plaintiff''s purchase price of 800 yuan; 2. The defendant shall pay the plaintiff tenfold compensation of 8000 yuan.',
    'Support', 'Food safety, online shopping, past the expiration date, refund one and compensate ten, ten times the purchase price, punitive damages'),

  ('case_f02', '(2025) Shanghai 0112 Civil First Instance No. 18900', 'Case of Wang Mou v. a Certain Trading Company: Dispute over an Online Shopping Contract (Imported Food Without Chinese Labels)', 'court_sh_minhang', 'Contract dispute', 'Online shopping contract disputes', '2025-11-10',
    'Plaintiff: Wang Mou (consumer); Defendant: a certain trading company (seller)',
    'When imported health food purchased online by a consumer had no Chinese-language label, the court found that it failed to meet food safety standards and supported compensation equal to ten times the purchase price.',
    'Wang Mou purchased imported health food for 1200 yuan. Upon delivery, the packaging had only foreign-language text, with no Chinese label or Chinese instructions. Wang Mou seeks a refund plus tenfold compensation.',
    'Under Article 97 of the Food Safety Law, imported prepackaged food must have Chinese labels and Chinese instructions; otherwise, it may not be imported and does not meet food safety standards. Under Article 148, consumers may claim compensation equal to ten times the purchase price. This case involves more than merely a "labeling defect that does not affect safety": the absence of a Chinese label prevents consumers from learning key information such as the ingredients and shelf life, affecting food safety and the right to know. Ten-times-price compensation of 1,200×10=12,000 yuan should therefore be awarded.',
    'Imported prepackaged food without a Chinese label or Chinese instructions does not meet food safety standards, and consumers may claim punitive damages equal to ten times the price paid.',
    '1. The defendant shall refund the purchase price of 1200 yuan; 2. The defendant shall pay tenfold compensation of 12000 yuan.',
    'Support', 'Food safety, imported food, no Chinese label, Chinese instructions, refund plus tenfold compensation, Article 97'),

  ('case_f03', '(2025) Shanghai 0115 Civil First-Instance No. 19980', 'Li Mou v. a Certain Food Company, Online Shopping Contract Dispute Case (a Guaranteed Minimum Punitive Compensation of 1,000 Yuan)', 'court_sh_pudong', 'Contract dispute', 'Online shopping contract disputes', '2025-10-20',
    'Plaintiff: Li Mou (consumer); Defendant: a certain food company (seller)',
    'When the purchase price of non-compliant food bought by a consumer was low and ten times the price was less than 1,000 yuan, the court supported punitive compensation subject to a minimum of 1,000 yuan.',
    'Li Mou purchased unpackaged nuts that did not meet food safety standards for 80 yuan. Ten times that amount is 800 yuan, which is less than 1,000 yuan. Li Mou claimed a refund of the purchase price plus tenfold compensation, with a minimum of 1,000 yuan.',
    'Pursuant to Article 148 of the Food Safety Law, where the amount of increased compensation is less than 1000 yuan, it shall be 1000 yuan. In this case, ten times the purchase price of 80 yuan is 800 yuan, which is less than 1000 yuan; punitive damages should therefore be awarded in the amount of 1000 yuan, in addition to refunding the purchase price of 80 yuan.',
    'If ten times the purchase price is less than 1,000 yuan, punitive compensation shall be calculated with a minimum of 1,000 yuan.',
    '1. The defendant shall refund the purchase price of 80 yuan; 2. The defendant shall pay punitive damages of 1000 yuan.',
    'Support', 'Food safety, ten times the purchase price, less than 1,000 yuan, 1,000-yuan minimum, punitive damages'),

  ('case_f04', '(2025) Shanghai 01 Civil Appellate Case No. 05600', 'A Food Company v. a Consumer—Appeal in an Online Shopping Contract Dispute (Compensation Still Available in Food Cases Even When the Buyer Knowingly Purchased Counterfeit or Substandard Food)', 'court_sh_no1', 'Contract dispute', 'Online shopping contract disputes', '2025-12-18',
    'Appellant: A certain food company (seller); Respondent: A certain consumer',
    'The seller argued that the consumer knowingly purchased food despite being aware of the problem (knowingly buying counterfeit goods), but the court of second instance held that knowingly buying counterfeit goods in the food sector does not affect the consumer''s right to seek compensation.',
    'The consumer repeatedly purchased the same substandard food and sought compensation. The seller argued that the consumer was a professional anti-counterfeiting claimant who knowingly purchased a product despite being aware of the problem, and that punitive damages should therefore not be awarded.',
    'Pursuant to Article 3 of the Supreme People''s Court Provisions on Issues Concerning the Application of Law in Food and Drug Disputes, in the food and drug sectors, where a producer or seller defends on the ground that the purchaser knowingly bought food despite knowing that it had quality problems, the people''s court shall not support the defense. In other words, in the food sector, knowingly purchasing counterfeit or defective products does not affect a consumer''s right to claim punitive damages under Article 148 of the Food Safety Law.',
    'In the food and drug sectors, whether purchasers knew about the issue (knowingly buying counterfeit goods) does not affect their right to claim tenfold punitive damages.',
    'I. Dismiss the appeal and uphold the original judgment (supporting tenfold compensation).',
    'Dismissed', 'Food safety, professional anti-counterfeiting claimant, food sector, punitive damages, Article 3'),

  ('case_f05', '(2025) Shanghai 0112 Civil First Instance No. 17200', 'Zhao v. a Certain E-Commerce Platform, Dispute over a Contract for Online Shopping (Platform Unable to Provide Seller Information · Advance Compensation)', 'court_sh_minhang', 'Contract dispute', 'Online shopping contract disputes', '2025-11-25',
    'Plaintiff: Zhao Mou (consumer); Defendant: a certain e-commerce platform',
    'The seller could not be contacted, and the platform was unable to provide the seller''s true information. The court ruled that the platform must first assume liability for compensating the consumer.',
    'After Zhao purchased substandard food online, the seller’s store closed and the seller became unreachable. The platform was unable to provide the seller’s true name, address, or valid contact information. Zhao requested compensation from the platform.',
    'Pursuant to Article 44 of the Law on the Protection of Consumers'' Rights and Interests and Article 6 of the Supreme People''s Court Provisions on Issues Concerning the Application of Law in Food and Drug Disputes, where an online trading platform cannot provide the seller''s true name, address, and valid contact information, the consumer may request that the platform assume liability for compensation; after paying compensation, the platform may seek indemnification from the seller.',
    'If an online trading platform cannot provide the consumer with the seller’s real information, the consumer may request that the platform first assume liability for compensation.',
    '1. The defendant platform shall bear liability to the plaintiff for refunding the purchase price and paying compensation equal to ten times that price; 2. After making the compensation, the platform may seek recourse from the seller.',
    'Support', 'Food safety, e-commerce platform, unable to provide seller information, advance compensation, recourse, Article 44'),

  ('case_f06', '(2025) Shanghai 0115 Civil First-Instance Case No. 20300', 'Qian v. a Food Company: Online Shopping Contract Dispute (Illegal Additives · Failure to Meet Safety Standards)', 'court_sh_pudong', 'Contract dispute', 'Online shopping contract disputes', '2025-10-30',
    'Plaintiff: Qian Mou (consumer); Defendant: a food company',
    'When food purchased by a consumer was found to contain illegal additives, the court found that it failed to meet food safety standards and supported compensation equal to ten times the purchase price.',
    'Qian purchased a certain tea substitute for 2000 yuan. Testing detected sibutramine and other non-food substances. Qian sought a refund plus tenfold compensation.',
    'Under Article 34 of the Food Safety Law, food containing chemical substances other than food additives or other substances that may endanger human health is prohibited from production and sale. Food found to contain illegal additives does not meet food safety standards. Under Article 148, ten-times-price compensation of 2,000×10=20,000 yuan should be awarded.',
    'If food is found to contain illegal additives or otherwise fails to comply with food-safety standards, the consumer may claim punitive compensation equal to ten times the purchase price.',
    '1. The defendant shall refund the purchase price of 2000 yuan; 2. The defendant shall pay tenfold compensation of 20000 yuan.',
    'Support', 'Food safety, illegal additives, sibutramine, failure to meet safety standards, refund plus tenfold compensation'),

  ('case_f07', '(2025) Shanghai 0112 Civil First Instance No. 16800', 'Sun Mou v. a Food Company, Dispute over an Online Shopping Contract (Label Defects Did Not Affect Safety · Tenfold Damages Not Awarded)', 'court_sh_minhang', 'Contract dispute', 'Online shopping contract disputes', '2025-09-15',
    'Plaintiff: Sun Mou (consumer); Defendant: a certain food company',
    'Where the food itself meets safety standards and only has defects such as label font size that do not affect safety and are not misleading, the court will not support a claim for tenfold compensation.',
    'The food purchased by Sun Mou met safety standards, but the producer''s address was printed in a font that was too small on the label, and there were a few punctuation errors. Sun Mou sought a refund plus tenfold damages.',
    'Pursuant to the proviso to Article 148 of the Food Safety Law and Article 15 of the Supreme People''s Court Provisions on Issues Concerning the Application of Law in Food and Drug Disputes, where food meets safety standards and the labels or instructions contain only defects that do not affect food safety and will not mislead consumers, a claim for tenfold punitive damages based on the purchase price shall not be supported. In this case, the defects in the typeface and punctuation do not affect safety and do not mislead consumers, so tenfold compensation does not apply; however, actual losses may be claimed separately.',
    'Where food complies with safety standards and its label contains only defects that do not affect safety or mislead consumers, tenfold punitive damages will not be awarded.',
    'I. Dismiss the plaintiff’s claim for tenfold punitive damages; II. The defendant may provide an explanation or replacement regarding the labeling defect.',
    'Dismissed', 'Food safety, labeling defect, does not affect safety, does not mislead consumers, tenfold damages not available, proviso'),

  ('case_f08', '(2025) Shanghai 0115 Civil First-Instance Case No. 21100', 'Zhou v. a Certain Food Company and a Certain Manufacturer, Online Shopping Contract Dispute Case (Producer or Seller, at Choice)', 'court_sh_pudong', 'Contract dispute', 'Online shopping contract disputes', '2025-09-28',
    'Plaintiff: Zhou (consumer); Defendants: a food company (seller) and a certain manufacturer',
    'For punitive damages arising from food that fails to meet safety standards, consumers may choose to seek compensation from either the producer or the seller, and the defendants may seek recourse from one another.',
    'The food purchased by Zhou was substandard, and both the manufacturer and the seller were defendants. Zhou claimed that both should be jointly and severally liable to pay ten times the compensation.',
    'Pursuant to Article 148 of the Food Safety Law, a consumer may demand ten times the purchase price from either the producer or the operator (seller), which is an alternative claim. In this case, the consumer may choose to claim all punitive damages from the seller; after making payment, the compensating party may seek indemnification from the party at fault under Article 1203 of the Civil Code. The producer and seller should not be ordered to bear joint and several liability for punitive damages unless circumstances giving rise to joint and several liability exist.',
    'For punitive damages arising from food that fails to meet safety standards, consumers may choose to seek compensation from either the producer or the seller, and the party that pays may seek recourse from the party at fault.',
    '1. The seller shall refund the purchase price and pay the plaintiff compensation equal to ten times that price; 2. After making the compensation, the seller may seek recourse from the manufacturer.',
    'Partially upheld', 'Food safety, producer, seller, either one, recourse, Article 1203'),

  ('case_f09', '(2024)Hu0115MinChu19100No.', 'Wu v. a Food Company: Online Shopping Contract Dispute (Three-Year Limitation Period)', 'court_sh_pudong', 'Contract dispute', 'Online shopping contract disputes', '2024-12-02',
    'Plaintiff: Wu (consumer); Defendant: a food company',
    'The seller argued that the statute of limitations had expired, but the court held that online shopping contract disputes are subject to the ordinary three-year limitation period, which had not expired.',
    'Wu purchased substandard food in 2022 and filed a lawsuit in 2024. The defendant argued that the limitation period had expired.',
    'Pursuant to Article 188 of the Civil Code, the ordinary limitation period for litigation is three years, commencing from the date when the rights holder knows or should have known both that the right had been infringed and who the obligor was. In this case, the three-year period commenced in 2022, when the purchase was made and the problem was discovered; filing suit in 2024 was within the three-year limitation period.',
    'Online shopping contract disputes are subject to the three-year general statute of limitations, calculated from the date on which the consumer knew or should have known that their rights had been harmed.',
    'I. Reject the defendant’s statute-of-limitations defense; II. The defendant shall bear liability to refund the purchase price and pay tenfold compensation.',
    'Support', 'Food safety, online shopping, limitation period, three years, ordinary limitation period'),

  ('case_f10', '(2025) Shanghai 0112 Civil First Instance No. 16200', 'Zheng v. a Food Company: Online Shopping Contract Dispute (Online Shopping Jurisdiction · Place of Receipt)', 'court_sh_minhang', 'Contract dispute', 'Online shopping contract disputes', '2025-07-18',
    'Plaintiff: Zheng Mou (consumer); Defendant: a food company (domiciled in Hangzhou, Zhejiang)',
    'The consumer sued the Hangzhou seller in Shanghai, the place of delivery, and the court held that the place of delivery under an online shopping contract was the place of performance and that it had jurisdiction.',
    'Zheng’s place of receipt was Shanghai, while the defendant seller’s domicile was Hangzhou, Zhejiang. The defendant argued that the Hangzhou court at its domicile should have jurisdiction.',
    'Pursuant to the Civil Procedure Law and its judicial interpretations, for a sales contract concluded through an information network, where the subject matter is delivered through the information network, the buyer''s place of residence is the place of performance of the contract; where the subject matter is delivered by other means, the place of receipt is the place of performance of the contract. The buyer''s (consumer''s) place of receipt, Shanghai, is the place of performance of the contract, so the Shanghai court has jurisdiction. The consumer may file suit at the place of receipt and need not go to the seller''s place of residence, Hangzhou.',
    'In online shopping contract disputes, the buyer’s place of receipt is the place of contract performance, and the court at that location has jurisdiction; consumers may sue at the place of receipt.',
    '1. This case falls under the jurisdiction of a certain district court in Shanghai at the place of receipt; 2. The defendant''s objection to jurisdiction is dismissed.',
    'Other', 'Food safety, online shopping, jurisdiction, place of receipt, place of contract performance, purchaser''s domicile'),

  ('case_f11', '(2025) Zhejiang 0110 Civil First-Instance Case No. 13900', 'A Consumer v. a Food Company—Online Shopping Contract Dispute (The Greater of Three Times the Loss or Ten Times the Purchase Price)', 'court_zj_hangzhou', 'Contract dispute', 'Online shopping contract disputes', '2025-08-22',
    'Plaintiff: a certain consumer; Defendant: a certain food company',
    'A consumer may choose between "ten times the purchase price" and "three times the loss," and the court will calculate the compensation in the manner more favorable to the consumer.',
    'The consumer paid 500 yuan for substandard food and incurred medical expenses of 2000 yuan. The consumer is claiming punitive damages.',
    'Under Article 148 of the Food Safety Law, consumers may demand compensation equal to ten times the purchase price (500×10=5,000 yuan) or three times their losses (2,000×3=6,000 yuan), choosing one of the two. The three-times-loss amount of 6,000 yuan, being more favorable to the consumer, should be awarded, together with compensation for the actual loss.',
    'Punitive damages may be calculated using either ten times the purchase price or three times the loss, whichever is more favorable to the consumer.',
    '1. The defendant shall pay compensation for the losses in an amount three times the losses, namely 6000 yuan; 2. The defendant shall refund the purchase price and compensate the actual losses.',
    'Support', 'Food safety, ten times the purchase price, three times the loss, choose one, choose the higher amount, punitive damages'),

  ('case_f12', '(2025) Shanghai 0115 Civil First-Instance Case No. 20600', 'A Consumer v. a Food Company—Online Shopping Contract Dispute (Threefold Damages for Fraud Involving Ordinary Goods; Distinguishing the Tenfold Remedy for Food)', 'court_sh_pudong', 'Contract dispute', 'Online shopping contract disputes', '2025-10-12',
    'Plaintiff: a certain consumer; Defendant: a certain food company',
    'Distinction: food safety issues are subject to tenfold compensation under the Food Safety Law, while general consumer fraud is subject to threefold compensation under the Consumer Rights Protection Law; this case concerns a food safety issue and is therefore subject to tenfold compensation.',
    'The consumer claims that the defendant sold food that did not comply with food safety standards, while the defendant argues that, at most, compensation should be three times the amount under the Consumer Protection Law.',
    'Punitive compensation in the food-safety sector is governed first by Article 148 of the Food Safety Law (ten times the purchase price / a minimum of 1,000 yuan), rather than the threefold compensation / 500 yuan under Article 55 of the Consumer Rights Protection Law. The latter applies to fraud involving general goods and services. This case concerns food that does not comply with food-safety standards, so the tenfold compensation applies rather than the threefold compensation.',
    'For food-safety issues, the tenfold punitive compensation under the Food Safety Law applies; the threefold compensation for fraud under the Consumer Rights Protection Law does not.',
    '1. The defendant shall pay compensation equal to ten times the purchase price; 2. The defendant''s defense seeking application of the threefold compensation standard is not supported.',
    'Partially upheld', 'Food safety, tenfold, threefold, Consumer Rights Protection Law, Food Safety Law prevails, distinguish'),

  ('case_f13', '(2025) Shanghai 0112 Civil First Instance No. 15800', 'A Certain Consumer v. a Certain Health Food Company, Online Shopping Contract Dispute Case (Health Food Masquerading as Ordinary Food and Claiming Efficacy)', 'court_sh_minhang', 'Contract dispute', 'Online shopping contract disputes', '2025-09-05',
    'Plaintiff: a certain consumer; Defendant: a certain health supplement company',
    'For ordinary food products that unlawfully claim to prevent or treat diseases and fail to comply with labeling requirements, courts support compensation of 10 times the purchase price.',
    'A certain product was sold as ordinary food, but its product page claimed that it could "treat high blood pressure and lower blood sugar" and displayed no health food approval number. The consumer claimed a refund of the purchase price plus tenfold compensation.',
    'Ordinary food products may not claim to prevent or treat diseases. Those that unlawfully claim such effects and fail to comply with labeling requirements are deemed not to meet food safety standards. Under Article 148 of the Food Safety Law, compensation of 10 times the purchase price is supported.',
    'For ordinary food products that unlawfully claim to prevent or treat diseases and fail to comply with labeling requirements, consumers may claim compensation of 10 times the purchase price.',
    '1. The defendant shall refund the purchase price; 2. The defendant shall pay compensation equal to ten times the purchase price.',
    'Support', 'Food safety, health food, efficacy claims, labeling, tenfold compensation'),

  ('case_f14', '(2025) Shanghai 0115 Civil First-Instance Case No. 21800', 'A Consumer v. an E-Commerce Platform—Online Shopping Contract Dispute (Platform Knew or Should Have Known; Joint and Several Liability)', 'court_sh_pudong', 'Tort liability', 'Online shopping contract disputes', '2025-11-15',
    'Plaintiff: a certain consumer; Defendants: a certain e-commerce platform and a certain seller',
    'Where a platform knows that a seller is selling substandard food but fails to take necessary measures, the court ruled that the platform and the seller bear joint and several liability.',
    'The consumer repeatedly complained that a store was selling substandard food. Even after the platform received the complaints and regulatory notices, it neither removed the products from sale nor took action.',
    'Pursuant to Article 44 of the Law on the Protection of Consumers'' Rights and Interests and Article 6 of the Supreme People''s Court Provisions on Issues Concerning the Application of Law in Food and Drug Disputes, where a platform knows or should know that a seller is using the platform to infringe consumers'' rights and interests but fails to take necessary measures, it shall bear joint and several liability with the seller. In this case, the platform received complaints and notifications but still failed to act, constituting a failure to take necessary measures despite having or being deemed to have knowledge; it should therefore bear joint and several liability for compensation.',
    'Where a platform knows or should know that a seller has infringed consumers'' rights and interests but fails to take necessary measures, it shall bear joint and several liability with the seller.',
    '1. The seller shall provide a refund and pay compensation equal to ten times the purchase price; 2. The platform and the seller shall bear joint and several liability.',
    'Support', 'Food safety, e-commerce platform, knew or should have known, failed to take necessary measures, joint and several liability'),

  ('case_f15', '(2025) Shanghai 0112 Civil First Instance No. 15300', 'A Consumer v. a Food Company—Online Shopping Contract Dispute (Preserving Evidence and Sealing Samples)', 'court_sh_minhang', 'Contract dispute', 'Online shopping contract disputes', '2025-06-20',
    'Plaintiff: a certain consumer; Defendant: a certain food company',
    'The consumer properly preserved the food product involved in the case, the order and payment records, and the chat records, and prevailed on the strength of sufficient evidence; conversely, the claim failed when the claimant could not prove the case.',
    'The consumer preserved the unopened food at issue, screenshots of the e-commerce order, proof of payment, chat records with customer service, and an unboxing video, using them to prove the purchase and the food-related problems.',
    'Where a consumer claims that food does not comply with food safety standards and seeks punitive compensation, the consumer bears the burden of proving the purchase, the food’s noncompliance with food safety standards, and other relevant facts. Properly preserving physical samples, orders, payment and communication records, unboxing videos, and other evidence is key to establishing the facts; where necessary, the consumer may apply for testing. If the evidence is insufficient, the corresponding claims are unlikely to be supported.',
    'A consumer seeking punitive compensation for food safety violations should preserve evidence such as physical samples, order, payment, and communication records, and apply for testing where necessary.',
    '1. The plaintiff''s evidence is sufficient; support a refund and tenfold compensation.',
    'Support', 'Food safety, evidence, physical samples, orders, unboxing videos, testing, burden of proof'),

  ('case_f16', '(2025) Shanghai 01 Civil Appellate Case No. 06100', 'A Food Company v. a Consumer—Appeal in an Online Shopping Contract Dispute (Inspection Institution Qualifications and Admissibility of the Report)', 'court_sh_no1', 'Contract dispute', 'Online shopping contract disputes', '2025-12-25',
    'Appellant: A certain food company; Respondent: A certain consumer',
    'An inspection report issued at one party’s own request by an institution lacking CMA/CNAS accreditation shall not be admitted; the inspection conducted by a qualified institution shall prevail.',
    'The consumer commissioned an institution to test the food involved in the case, and the seller challenged whether the institution was qualified to conduct food testing.',
    'Whether food fails to meet safety standards involves specialized issues, so testing should be conducted by an institution qualified to perform food testing (with CMA qualification certification and, where necessary, CNAS accreditation). A test report issued by an institution without the corresponding qualifications and commissioned independently by a party has questionable evidentiary value and generally will not be directly admitted by the court; testing should be conducted by a qualified institution or commissioned by the court. Choosing an inappropriate testing institution will result in the report not being admitted.',
    'Food testing shall be conducted by institutions with CMA/CNAS qualifications; reports from unqualified institutions will not be accepted.',
    '1. The opinion of a qualified institution shall prevail; 2. Uphold the finding supporting punitive damages.',
    'Dismissed', 'Food safety, testing institution, CMA, CNAS, qualifications, acceptance of the report'),

  ('case_f17', '(2024)Zhe0110MinChu18700No.', 'A Consumer v. a Food Company—Online Shopping Contract Dispute (Excessive Claim; Far Exceeding Reasonable Daily Consumption Needs)', 'court_zj_hangzhou', 'Contract dispute', 'Online shopping contract disputes', '2024-12-02',
    'Plaintiff: a certain consumer; Defendant: a certain food company',
    'Where a party purchases and stockpiles a large quantity far exceeding reasonable household consumption needs, the court will cautiously determine any claim for tenfold compensation for the excess portion.',
    'The purchaser bought hundreds of units of the same substandard food product in a single transaction and seeks compensation equal to ten times the total purchase price.',
    'Knowingly purchasing counterfeit food does not affect the right to seek compensation. However, for large stockpiling purchases that clearly exceed reasonable household consumption needs and are made by persons who make a profession of seeking compensation, some judgments cautiously determine punitive damages equal to ten times the purchase price for the portion exceeding a reasonable consumption quantity, so as to balance punishment with the prevention of abuse of rights; the tenfold damages are still supported for quantities within the scope of reasonable consumption.',
    'For bulk purchases that clearly exceed reasonable household consumption needs, tenfold compensation for the excess portion may be cautiously determined.',
    '1. Support tenfold compensation within reasonable consumption quantities; 2. Exercise caution in handling clearly excessive quantities.',
    'Partially upheld', 'Food safety, knowingly buying counterfeit goods, reasonable personal consumption, stockpiling purchases, prudence, abuse of rights'),

  ('case_f18', '(2025) Shanghai 0115 Civil First-Instance Case No. 20100', 'A Consumer v. an Importer—Online Shopping Contract Dispute (Imported Food Lacking a Certificate of Conformity or Inspection and Quarantine Documentation)', 'court_sh_pudong', 'Contract dispute', 'Online shopping contract disputes', '2025-08-30',
    'Plaintiff: a certain consumer; Defendant: a certain importer',
    'Imported food lacked a Certificate of Inspection and Quarantine for Inbound Goods and other required conformity documents; the court held that it failed to meet food safety standards and awarded tenfold compensation.',
    'For imported food purchased by a consumer, the seller was unable to provide entry inspection and quarantine certificates or documents proving conformity.',
    'Imported food should obtain certificates of conformity from entry-exit inspection and quarantine authorities, among others. Imported food for which a certificate of conformity cannot be provided and whose source is unknown cannot be proven to comply with China''s food safety standards; pursuant to Article 148 of the Food Safety Law, punitive damages equal to ten times the price paid shall be awarded.',
    'Imported food without a certificate of conformity from entry-exit inspection and quarantine authorities or other required certificates cannot be proven to meet safety standards, and tenfold compensation shall be awarded.',
    '1. The defendant shall refund the purchase price; 2. The defendant shall pay compensation equal to ten times the purchase price.',
    'Support', 'Food safety, imported food, inspection and quarantine, certificate of conformity, unknown origin, tenfold');

