   'The consumer filed a lawsuit over an online shopping contract concerning an interruption in the cold chain, and the court ruled after considering the nature of the food and the evidence of the transaction.', 'After purchasing snack foods online, the consumer discovered a cold-chain interruption. Temperature control during transportation of the refrigerated food was abnormal, and the consumer claimed that the product was no longer safe. The consumer retained the order, payment records, unboxing photos, and communication records.', 'The court held that this case should first distinguish between ordinary defects in labeling or advertising and noncompliance rising to the level of food safety. The ruling addressed logistics records, storage and transportation requirements, and food safety standards. It also assessed the matter in light of the burden of proof, trade practices, and consumers’ reasonable reliance.', 'Regarding cold-chain interruption issues, the court emphasized that the determination should take into account the specific food category, mandatory information-disclosure obligations, and the actual extent to which consumers were affected.', '1. Partially support the claims concerning cold-chain interruptions; 2. Handle the remaining claims based on the evidence presented.', 'Support', 'Food safety, online shopping, cold-chain interruption, snacks' );


   'The consumer filed a lawsuit over an online shopping contract dispute concerning inadequate allergen labeling, and the court ruled by taking into account the nature of the food and the transaction evidence.', 'After purchasing a honey product online, the consumer discovered that allergen information was inadequately disclosed. The packaging did not sufficiently indicate allergen information, and the consumer claims that the label contained a material omission. The consumer retained the order, payment records, unboxing photographs, and communication records.', 'The court held that this case should first distinguish between ordinary defects in labeling or advertising and noncompliance rising to the level of food safety. The court emphasized mandatory information disclosure and consumers’ ability to identify risks. It also assessed the matter in light of the burden of proof, trade practices, and consumers’ reasonable reliance.', 'Regarding inadequate allergen warnings, the ruling emphasized that the determination should be made in light of the specific food category, mandatory information disclosure obligations, and the actual extent to which consumers were affected.', '1. The claims concerning inadequate allergen labeling are partially supported; 2. The remaining claims will be handled according to the evidence presented.', 'Support', 'Food safety, online shopping, insufficient allergen warnings, honey' );


